  "question": {
    "text": "In a thermodynamic process, the pressure of a fixed mass of a gas is changed in such a manner that the gas releases $20 \\mathrm{~J}$ of heat and $8 \\mathrm{~J}$ of work is done on the gas. If the initial internal energy of the gas was $30 \\mathrm{~J}$, then the final internal energy will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$42 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$18 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$58 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\Delta \\mathrm{Q}=-20 \\mathrm{~J}, \\mathrm{~W}=-8 \\mathrm{~J}$\r\n\r\nUsing Ist law $\\Delta \\mathrm{Q}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}+\\Delta \\mathrm{W}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\Delta Q=-20+8=-12 \\mathrm{~J} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{Uf}=-12+30=18 \\mathrm{~J}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$"
  }
}